THIRD-PARTY NOTICES

This package contains no source code from other software.  Its algorithms are
implemented from the published literature; each source file names the papers it
follows, and docs/src/theory.md lists them in full.  The principal ones are:

* Laplacian pyramid: P. J. Burt and E. H. Adelson, IEEE Trans. Commun. 31(4),
  1983.
* CDF 9/7 filters: A. Cohen, I. Daubechies and J.-C. Feauveau, Commun. Pure Appl.
  Math. 45(5), 1992.
* Directional filter bank: R. H. Bamberger and M. J. T. Smith, IEEE Trans. Signal
  Process. 40(4), 1992; M. N. Do, PhD thesis, EPFL, 2001.
* "23-45" (pkva) quincunx filters: S.-M. Phoong, C. W. Kim, P. P. Vaidyanathan
  and R. Ansari, IEEE Trans. Signal Process. 43(3), 1995.
* Contourlet transform: M. N. Do and M. Vetterli, IEEE Trans. Image Process.
  14(12), 2005.
* Nonsubsampled contourlet transform: A. L. da Cunha, J. Zhou and M. N. Do, IEEE
  Trans. Image Process. 15(10), 2006.
* Translation-invariant and semi-translation-invariant contourlet transforms:
  R. Eslami and H. Radha, IEEE Trans. Image Process. 15(11), 2006; the
  Laplacian pyramid as an oversampled filter bank: M. N. Do and M. Vetterli,
  IEEE Trans. Signal Process. 51(9), 2003.

The MATLAB Contourlet Toolbox (M. N. Do et al.; GNU General Public License) and
the Nonsubsampled Contourlet Toolbox (A. L. da Cunha, J. Zhou and M. N. Do; no
licence stated) are neither included in nor derived into this package.  They are
used only as black-box reference programs: the scripts under matlab/ run them to
compare outputs and timings, and test/reference/toolbox_dfb_l12.bin holds output
produced by running the Contourlet Toolbox (see test/reference/README.md).
